await sharp({create:{width:3072,height:1668,channels:3,background:'#101216'}}).composite([{input:await readFile(versionDir(18)+'sheet.png'),left:0,top:0},{input:await readFile(dir+'sheet.png'),left:1536,top:0}]).png().toFile(dir+'l18-l19-side-by-side.png');
await writeFile(dir+'notes.md',`# l19: HERITAGE dust\n\n**${retained?'Retained':'Rejected; retain l18'}**. ${decision.reason}\n\nHERITAGE BEMBB provides 56-arcsecond sampled dust-density structure. Full-column replacement failed the tiny guard. The final controlled candidate applies its finer-than-five-arcminute modulation to the parent diffuse column, preserves the finite molecular clouds, and restores Bell's combined mean using one diffuse normalization. This is a fine-structure reconciliation, not acceptance of the raw HERITAGE coarse column.\n\nBell's mean vertical V optical depth is ${f(norm.bellMeanFaceOnTauV)}; the combined normalized field gives ${f(norm.afterMeanFaceOnTauV)}. The fitted global dust strength is ${num(result.dustStrength).toFixed(3)}, within 0.25–2. The layer remains 250 pc on the existing warp, with the unchanged Gordon RGB extinction response. Stellar geometry, light, colors and the display curve stay at l18.\n\n| Bar texture, 2–5 arcmin | Photo | l18 | l19 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Log-luminance band power | ${num(p.power).toExponential(5)} | ${num(a.power).toExponential(5)} | ${num(b.power).toExponential(5)} |\n| Dark-feature power | ${num(p.darkPower).toExponential(5)} | ${num(a.darkPower).toExponential(5)} | ${num(b.darkPower).toExponential(5)} |\n\nThese use the same fixed catalogue-masked bar and mask-normalized Gaussian filters with 2 and 5 arcminute FWHM. Native photo samples are area-averaged; the crop inherits the full image's sky and display scale. One-arcminute modes are not claimed from a 56-arcsecond sampled density map.\n\n| Whole-image RGB RMS | l18 | l19 | Change |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n${row('trainRelativeRms','First checkerboard')}\n${row('heldoutRelativeRms','Second checkerboard')}\n\nThe declared limit is +1% relative on either residual. Both tiny residuals increased beyond that guard; the native diagnostic cannot overturn that failure. These are calibration residuals, not independent validation.\n\n[Method](method.md), [visual review](visual-review.md), [sheet](sheet.png), [comparison](l18-l19-side-by-side.png) and [bar crop](bar-close-up.png). Tiny took ${num(rungs[0].seconds).toFixed(1)} seconds. The native sheet took ${num(result.seconds).toFixed(1)} seconds, with additional frozen crop rendering. No full-resolution fit or slab bake ran.\n`);
const path=ROOT+'src/objects/lmc-volume/source/preparation/l19/recipe.json',recipe=rec(await json(path));await writeFile(path,JSON.stringify({...recipe,generatorArguments:rec(cfg.details).diagnosticRejected===true?['--diagnostic-rejected']:[],decision},null,2)+'\n');console.log(JSON.stringify({sentinel:'L19_REPORTED',...decision}));
